+++
title: Yomonsni
+++

“The undiscovered life is not worth living.”

Many of us have heard that sentiment before. But what does it actually mean to discover ourselves? Is it a destination we arrive at, or a practice we maintain? 

Mark Twain once said: “I can tell anyone how to get exactly what they want. The problem is I can’t find anybody who knows what they want.”

That is where we come in.


The Collective
We are a collective of facilitators who believe that success looks different for everyone. We do not sell you a structured path to a destination we define. We want to help you to understand who you are, what you really want, and to help you get there. 

We are not gatekeepers of knowledge. There are incredible resources out there for you to read and watch in nearly any domain you choose. We even write some of our own perspectives on a range of different topics. We also share some of the things we find most valuable as a collection of resources within each of the domains, or focus areas below. You can take the resources, reading lists, and behavioral pointers we share and go it alone. Or, you can bring a coach into the conversation.

Because the truth is: We would all benefit an external perspective

All the coaches in this collective work to coach each other regularly. We are all students of the human experience. We are here for the interactive discussion, the “intentional experimentation,” and the honest feedback that helps you see past your own blind spots. We can push past the surface answers and help you to find the real truth within yourself.


Our objective
We want to help you find out who you are, what you want, and to show you that there's much less holding you back than you imagine. 

Whether it is the grit of an athlete striving for elite performance, the presence of a leader trying to bring others into their vision, helping a creator to find their voice in their work, helping you to discover how to understand yourself and break free of cultural loading on your intimate self, or how to discover and articulate your full sense of self and purpose, our work is about discovering and building you. We don’t look back to heal old wounds; we look forward to build new tools. Take a look at <a href="coaching.html">our view on coaching</a> to understand this in more detail.

While we support work on the whole person (it's what we do ourselves), we are also able to meet you where you're at and help you with the challenges that you are working on right now. Explore the domains below, and the coaches that we have who work in each domain. Read what we have to say, what our past clients may have to say about us, and decide if we can help you. Whether just through coaching sessions (online and in person), or through our workshops, or through our individual or small group retreat intensives, we want to support your growth.

We invite you to Observe, Experiment, Reflect, Integrate and Connect. 



